Network provider deadline coverage
==================================

provider_test uses real capability channels and local sockets. Its loopback
bind/connect cases require 127.0.0.1 to be configured. The disposable native
runtime fixture now supplies that address without an external network adapter.
Provider policy identities and startup remain fixture inputs, so passing this
suite does not prove SwitchBoard admission or installed bundle activation.

provider_connect_timeout_expires attempts to create an unresponsive peer by
saturating a local listen queue. Kernels that refuse the extra connection
immediately cannot satisfy that precondition; the case explicitly skips.
The native runner treats skips as failures. Keep this real stalled-peer gate
pending until a suitable isolated packet-loss fixture is available.

connect_deadline_test calls the production broker_perform_connect helper with
injected connect, poll and monotonic-clock operations and real socket fcntl
state. It verifies that EINTR does not restart the timeout, timeout and poll
errors survive cleanup, and both initially blocking and nonblocking sockets
retain their original flags on failure and successful completion. This is
control-flow coverage, not a wall-clock latency or real TCP timeout result.
